The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (not_2): not(true) = false.
Axiom 2 (isGT_3): isGT(gt) = true.
Axiom 4 (compareNat_3): compareNat(suc(X), zero) = gt.
Axiom 5 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
Axiom 6 (maxNat_case1_2): maxNat_case1(false, X, Y) = X.
Axiom 7 (leNat_1): leNat(X, Y) = not(isGT(compareNat(X, Y))).
Axiom 8 (prop_maxLeft_case1_2): prop_maxLeft_case1(false, X, Y) = eqNat(maxNat(Y, X), X).
Axiom 9 (prop_maxLeft_1): prop_maxLeft(X, Y) = prop_maxLeft_case1(leNat(X, Y), Y, X).
Axiom 10 (maxNat_1): maxNat(X, Y) = maxNat_case1(leNat(X, Y), X, Y).

Lemma 11: leNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
Proof:
  leNat(suc(X), zero)
= { by axiom 7 (leNat_1) }
  not(isGT(compareNat(suc(X), zero)))
= { by axiom 4 (compareNat_3) }
  not(isGT(gt))
= { by axiom 2 (isGT_3) }
  not(true)
= { by axiom 1 (not_2) }
  false

Goal 1 (prop_maxLeft): prop_maxLeft(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = suc(X)
  Y = zero

Proof:
  prop_maxLeft(suc(X), zero)
= { by axiom 9 (prop_maxLeft_1) }
  prop_maxLeft_case1(leNat(suc(X), zero), zero, suc(X))
= { by lemma 11 }
  prop_maxLeft_case1(false, zero, suc(X))
= { by axiom 8 (prop_maxLeft_case1_2) }
  eqNat(maxNat(suc(X), zero), zero)
= { by axiom 10 (maxNat_1) }
  eqNat(maxNat_case1(leNat(suc(X), zero), suc(X), zero), zero)
= { by lemma 11 }
  eqNat(maxNat_case1(false, suc(X), zero), zero)
= { by axiom 6 (maxNat_case1_2) }
  eqNat(suc(X), zero)
= { by axiom 5 (eqNat_3) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
